  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : "The CVODE is a package written in C that solves ODE initial value problems, in real N-space, written as y'=f(t,y),  y(t0)=y0. It is capable for stiff and non-stiff systems and uses two different linear multi-step methods, namely the Adam-Moulton [http://identifiers.org/biomodels.kisao/KISAO_0000280] method and the backward differentiation formula [http://identifiers.org/biomodels.kisao/KISAO_0000288]."
